# module set is given in full per step.
# pool_attacked: vram
#
# basis      s0 decomposition (steps/s0_default/peak-objects.md), re-derived 2026-08-02 on the full
#            H200 (line re-measured after leaving the MIG slice). W_vram 36.25, W_host 12.84 -> VRAM.
#              cuda_tensor.py:255:matmul <- __torch_function__ <- beaver.py:82:__beaver_protocol
#              2850.4 MB, 39.9% of the 6.65 GiB peak, 50.5% of what the decomposition attributed
#            same object and size on MIG slice and full card (device peak 6971392 kB on both); wall
#            51 to 57 s vs 99 to 108 s.
# object     CUDALongTensor.matmul: int64 split into 4 fp64 limbs, 4x4 cross-product as one batched
#            fp64 matmul ([16, ...] at once). Next three VRAM objects (cuda_tensor.py:610/254/249,
#            713.0 + 475.1 + 118.8 MB) belong to the same product; four together 73.6% attributed.
# lever      limb products one at a time, shift and accumulate; one product live.
# cost       up to ten sequential matmuls; measured +6.2% against a corrected wall spread of 25.4%
#            (host node shared; GPU exclusive): cost_type free, under-resolved; needs a dedicated A/B.
# note       embed_chunk_gpu.py:61 in the baseline table is a call frame only (SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS
#            unset in RUN_META; module imported unconditionally, no-op).
#
